From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The follower Pokémon (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OPTIONS: ENHANCEMENTS: FOLLOWER (PORT_OPT_FOLLOWER, off by default): the
party's first Pokémon walks behind the player (port_follower.c).

Its sprite: HeartGold and SoulSilver's when the player's data pack has
them (builder/followers.py: a port file at PORT_FOLLOWER_PAK_ID, each laid
out as Platinum's walking sprites), else Platinum's own for the 24 it has.
HeartGold's are graphics IDs of their own (PORT_FOLLOWER_GFX_FIRST + 2 *
sprite + shiny; from 0x4000): their texture a member of the overworld sprites' archive
past its own (narc.c: PortFollower_NarcMember; the shiny one with its two
palettes swapped), drawn as Pikachu is (Regigigas for 64 x 64) with
Platinum's walk (ov5_021ECE40.c, ov5_021ECC20.c, map_object.c lookups).

It is a map object (MAP_OBJ_STATUS_PORT_FOLLOWER, local ID 0xF3) moving
with MOVEMENT_TYPE_FOLLOW_PLAYER's code under a movement type of its own
(PORT_MOVEMENT_TYPE_FOLLOW_MON), so scripts never take it for the partner
trainer: walked through, kept across zone changes, never saved, not
talked to. Out when the player walks (not on the bike, surfing or using
a field move), with no partner trainer or Amity Square's Pokémon, outside
the Underground, the Union Room and maps with features of their own; a
64 x 64 one only outdoors. Not an egg, not fainted. Out behind the player
when that tile is free, else on the player's tile hidden till they step
off it (walking out of a door: it comes out after them). Back in its ball
when not to be out, another Pokémon is first, the game moves the player
(a script's walk: out again when the player is theirs again), it's left
behind (a warp within the map), or the player jumps down a ledge (the
follow code can't keep up with the jump): out again behind the player
where they stop. Its graphics IDs from 0x4000, past the berry
trees' (0x1000) and OBJ_EVENT_GFX_INVISIBLE (0x2000).

Its Poké Ball: coming out it grows from nothing (its picture made at no
size: ov5_021ECE40.c, PortFollower_StartsSmall), going in it shrinks
away where it stands, 6 frames each, with the battle's send-out and
recall sounds. Those are in the battle's sound bank, which the field
never loads: the field's sound effects load them too (sound.c), the
sound heap 128 kB larger for their 84 kB of waves (sound_system.h). It
comes and goes as set while the options' page is up (the field running
behind it, patch 0057).
